ttps://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114434","id":3698214993,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7cbkhR","user":{"login":"RealMadvicius","id":77865890,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3ODY1ODkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/77865890?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius","html_url":"https://github.com/RealMadvicius","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RealMadvicius/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-30T03:41:15Z","updated_at":"2025-12-30T03:41:15Z","body":"> Have you reproduced any of these theoretical crashes in practice? I see a few false positives already from a quick look at the code.\r\n> \r\n> It's not good practice to throw null checks everywhere just for the sake of it.\r\n\r\nHello, as I have mentioned in the issue ticket I have created ( so there is is traceability for the PR ), I wanted to check the output of static code analysis with CppCheck set to level \"exhaustive\" and warning level 4. I picked the category for null pointers dereference and gave a look at the list it gave to me, there where several false positive ( most likely it couldnt expand properly certain macro ) and thus didn't see that some checks were made. But there are some others I could spot and showed to Lyuma aswell who told me to make a PR.\r\nFor example the case in basisu_comp.cpp where it calls \"pSource_images\" instead of pSource_images_hdr in an obvious crash since in that section the pSource_images will always be null.\r\nSadly I don't have a project to reproduce crashes, only observations on pointers not guarded that could trigger a crash.\r\nI can clean some if they are judged as false positive though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3698214993/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]